dless  to say he plays a big role in season 1  and even has a few cameos in season 8's  apocalypse in the kitchen they're  greeted with some wine black rose petals  and a card that says welcome to murder  house which is also the title of the  very first episode of american horror  story connie reads the back of the note  referring to violetators which is a  mashup of the names violet and tate who  are lovers in season one they head on  upstairs to what was once tate langdon  and violet's room dylan even puts on the  iconic tate langdon sweater to get  connie in the mood but ends up lasting  as long as one of my relationships they  notice that all these candles have been  lit and surmise that someone must be in  the house to facilitate the scares they  even joke it could be larry harvey  dennis o'hare's character from season 1  who burned his family alive in murder  house we hear adelaide langdon's voice  call out you're going to die and hear  one of her iconic lines from season 1 as  well as beau langdon's red ball roll in  something we also saw in episode 1 of  this season yet we never see beau they  find the body of nurse gladys a murdered  character from season 1 who also makes  an appearance in the first two episodes  of stories but they believe this all to  be a part of the horror experience they  even remark how it must have been serial  killer richard speck who killed the  nurse which is a callback to the  character he inspired in season 1 r  franklin who killed nurses after a  thermometer broke in his mouth and this  is where we get our first glimpse of the  season-going meta which some have  criticized connie's character says of  season five's roanoke why does sarah  paulson should talk this season the show  has now become a commentary unto itself  this is later expanded upon by the  character of rory who talks about how  he's an hs super fan and only super fans  understand what american horror story is  some have criticized this as creators  ryan murphy and brad falchuk's poking  fun at the fandom by purposely creating  an annoying whiny brat as their  representation of the fandom and i kind  of get it i've done videos rewriting the  endings of both apocalypse and 1984  because i didn't like them but what i  think they miss here is that it comes  from a place of love i love the show so  much regardless it's always dangerous  when you bite the hand that feeds i want  to hear what you guys thought about this  in the comments below moving on we meet  these three new girls who were killed 10  years ago by the rubber man and piggy  man even after ben harmon warned them  they should go and dylan mcdermott who  plays dr harmon is the biggest cameo we  get in this episode he having played dr  ben harmon in season 1 reprised it in  season 8 was season 2's johnny morgan  and was last seen as another killer  bruce in 1984. but for those keen eyed  viewers out there you'll notice some  inconsistencies starting to form number  one piggy man never actually was a  character that died in murder house he  was a figment of one of ben harmon's  patience derek number two if the murders  of these three women happened 10 years  ago how is ruby here she only became a  ghost of murder house in 2020. number  three just really really bad cgi blood  which most times ahs goes for the real  thing with some exceptions thankfully  these inconsistencies are rectified when  we learn everything we've been watching  in this introductory segment is part of  a video game hence the title game over  the infantada another character from  season one who is pieced together using  the remains of charles and norah  montgomery's dead child slashes dylan  and connie as they make their escape we  get more fan service with adelaide  langdon returning saying i told you dumb  [ __ ] you're gonna die in here yet  another inconsistency since adelaide  died off of the property in season 1 and  thus would never have returned as a  ghost budget twisty is here too along  